  "narrative": "All newly delivered estimates are already signed for direction -1, so positive values favor the registered hypothesis that the exposed group or subgroup contrast has a more negative outcome score, i.e. stronger dependency. I used outcome-specific approximate 10 percent practical thresholds: about 0.0093 for outcome_006 and outcome_014, 0.025 for many outcome_012-scale outcomes, 0.027 for outcome_013, 0.028 for outcome_008, and 0.030 for outcome_011. No new discovery-only result is strong enough to accept. The main unresolved line is outcome_014 among feature_002=0 cases. H141 interaction by feature_034 is positive (+0.0507, interval -0.0383 to +0.1397), H143 feature_034 main effect within feature_002=0 is positive but uncertain (+0.0191, -0.0254 to +0.0637), and H142 complement is small and imprecise (+0.0079, -0.0567 to +0.0725). These patterns are compatible with a localized outcome_014 effect but are not established because intervals include null and lower bounds are below practical thresholds; they are also post-hoc subgroup/interaction tests with multiple comparisons. H144 tests feature_061 modification of the accepted feature_060/outcome_006 association and is positive but extremely imprecise (+0.0377, -0.0653 to +0.1408); together with prior non-replicating median-stratum screens it does not support clinically stable effect modification, so reject and close. New screens H145, H146, H35, H60, H72, and H73 show opposite, near-null, or clinically unsupported associations and are rejected/closed. H67, feature_011 and outcome_006, is the most interesting new screen: positive +0.0264, above threshold but interval -0.0181 to +0.0709 and not validated; keep active as a secondary lead. H147, the feature_002 main effect on outcome_006, is near null (+0.0078, -0.0246 to +0.0402); it is insufficient for acceptance and deferred for context. I request independent validation of H37 because it is the broader direct outcome_014 feature_060 comparison within feature_002=0, with prior discovery +0.0340 and larger cells than the localized tests; this is the decisive next step for the outcome_014 lead. All statements remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or externally generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Accepted: H15 only. Validation request now: H37, outcome_014 feature_060 within feature_002=0; one independent validation request remains afterward. Keep outcome_014 line active pending H37 validation: H141 is positive but uncertain interaction by feature_034, H143 is positive but uncertain feature_034 main effect within feature_002=0, H142 is near-null complement, and H130/H129 remain localized/interaction leads. If H37 validates with clinically meaningful positive effect for outcome_014 (threshold about 0.0093), consider accepting H37 as a dataset-specific association and decide whether final validation should test H130/H141 localization or move to H67; if H37 validation is null, opposite, or not clinically meaningful, close H37/H129/H130/H141/H142 and avoid further outcome_014 feature_060/feature_034 localization. H67 is secondary active lead: outcome_006 feature_011=1 vs 0, signed +0.0264, interval -0.0181 to +0.0709; if H37 fails, or if final validation remains after H37 succeeds, validate H67 before acceptance. H147 feature_002 main effect on outcome_006 is deferred near-null context; do not expand feature_002 main-effect screens. Closed new lines: H144 feature_061 modification of accepted H15; H145 feature_019/outcome_006; H146 feature_055/outcome_014; H35 feature_045/outcome_014; H60 feature_054/outcome_012; H72 feature_035/outcome_013; H73 feature_022/outcome_008. Practical thresholds follow approximately 10 percent of mean absolute dependency score: outcome_006/outcome_014 0.0093, outcome_008 0.028, outcome_001 0.042, outcome_013 0.027, outcome_011 0.030, most other central outcome scores about 0.025. Do not accept discovery-only subgroup or interaction claims unless magnitude and uncertainty are informative and ideally validated. All conclusions are dataset-specific associational statements, not causal effects or generalizable biology.",
